# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile instead of
# back/.dockerignore. The context is back/, but auth-gateway only needs the
# generated Go code and its own directory: everything else (the legacy
# prototype in _legacy/, gen/python, proto/, deploy/, .git, other
# services, local .env files) stays out of the build context.
*
!gen/go/
!services/auth-gateway/

**/.env
**/.env.*
# Signing keys are mounted at run time, never copied into an image.
services/auth-gateway/secrets/
services/auth-gateway/bin/
services/auth-gateway/*.test
services/auth-gateway/coverage.*
